This SlackBuild provides a quick way to install kongarena. It installs to /opt, and will make /opt/kong_arena/bin writeable by all users, but leaves the roms read-only.

You can change options (e.g. key or joystick inputs, audio, etc.) directly by running kong_arena/bin/dkwolf_linux then changing options manually and hitting 'save configuration'.

An alternative way to add controller support is the following:
0) In kong_arena/bin/extra_args.txt add "-ctrlr kongarena" to the end of the first line
1) Add the empty folder kong_arena/bin/ctrlr
2) Add the file kongarena.cfg to the ctrlr folder, adjusting your joystick buttons as necessary

-----

As an alternative to using SlackBuild, I will leave these older instructions for posterity.
These instructions should also work in most linux distributions.
To run KongArena (for a single user) from your desktop, you can do the following:

0) Download KongArena-Linux-x64.tar.gz from kongarena.com
1) 'tar xf KongArena-Linux-x64.tar.gz' (extract the files as your user) and then, as root, move the resulting kong_arena folder into /opt
2) Put kongarena.desktop in /usr/share/applications/
3) put kongarena in /usr/games and make it executable (chmod a+x)

You should then be able to type 'kongarena' in terminal, or click on the shortcut in your desktop menu.
